DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     An application is allowed to monitor the thread context switches inside
     the threading library.  An application can install a routine that gets
     called every time a thread (explicitly created by an application with the
     pthread_create(3) function) gets the context switched.  The routine is
     passed the thread IDs of the threads that are being switched in and out.
     Installation and removal of these hooks may be done using the
     pptthhrreeaadd__sswwiittcchh__aadddd__nnpp() and pptthhrreeaadd__sswwiittcchh__ddeelleettee__nnpp() functions respec‐
     tively.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, these functions return 0.  Otherwise, an error number is
     returned to indicate the error.

